 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` resolves a string-form JSON Pointer from RFC 6901 and returns the
+referenced value. The empty string selects the whole document. A non-empty pointer must begin with `/`;
+within each path token, `~1` decodes to `/` and `~0` decodes to `~`. Object properties must exist as
+own properties. Array tokens must be decimal indices without leading zeroes (except `0`) and must
+identify an existing element. Invalid pointer syntax and paths that do not resolve throw an error.
